 "text": "Hello, how are you doing today? Sure, a complementary color is one that opposite it on the color wheel. It gives a strong contrast and can make your main color stand out. In painting, light reflects back out of a surface in certain areas, and colors next to each other on the color wheel absorb each other's light. Exactly. It gives you the effect of light hitting the surface without making it look dead. You won't regret it. Complementary colors add so much energy to a painting.",
